{
  "total": 879.765,
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "S01",
      "start": 0.4,
      "speech_end": 4.01,
      "end": 4.81,
      "dur": 4.41,
      "text": "Somewhere in every clothing shop there is an invisible line."
    },
    {
      "id": "S02",
      "start": 4.81,
      "speech_end": 6.95,
      "end": 7.75,
      "dur": 2.94,
      "text": "On one side of it, a sign says MEN."
    },
    {
      "id": "S02b",
      "start": 7.75,
      "speech_end": 9.21,
      "end": 10.01,
      "dur": 2.26,
      "text": "On the other side, WOMEN."
    },
    {
      "id": "S03",
      "start": 10.01,
      "speech_end": 15.6,
      "end": 16.4,
      "dur": 6.39,
      "text": "Nobody guards that line. Nobody asks to see your papers when you step across it."
    },
    {
      "id": "S04",
      "start": 16.4,
      "speech_end": 19.81,
      "end": 20.61,
      "dur": 4.21,
      "text": "And yet almost everybody knows exactly where it runs."
    },
    {
      "id": "S05",
      "start": 20.61,
      "speech_end": 24.1,
      "end": 24.9,
      "dur": 4.29,
      "text": "This is men's clothing. That is women's clothing."
    },
    {
      "id": "S05b",
      "start": 24.9,
      "speech_end": 28.337,
      "end": 29.137,
      "dur": 4.237,
      "text": "This colour is masculine. That one is feminine."
    },
    {
      "id": "S06",
      "start": 29.137,
      "speech_end": 31.037,
      "end": 31.837,
      "dur": 2.7,
      "text": "So somebody must have drawn it."
    },
    {
      "id": "S07",
      "start": 31.837,
      "speech_end": 36.895,
      "end": 37.695,
      "dur": 5.858,
      "text": "Some committee. Some international body. The Ministry of Trousers, perhaps."
    },
    {
      "id": "S07b",
      "start": 37.695,
      "speech_end": 38.889,
      "end": 39.689,
      "dur": 1.995,
      "text": "There isn't one."
    },
    {
      "id": "S08",
      "start": 39.689,
      "speech_end": 44.679,
      "end": 45.479,
      "dur": 5.79,
      "text": "There is no authority anywhere that decides what counts as men's clothing and women's."
    },
    {
      "id": "S08b",
      "start": 45.479,
      "speech_end": 49.149,
      "end": 49.949,
      "dur": 4.469,
      "text": "No committee. No register. No standard. No inspector."
    },
    {
      "id": "S09",
      "start": 49.949,
      "speech_end": 55.619,
      "end": 56.419,
      "dur": 6.47,
      "text": "The rules are real enough that breaking one gets you stared at. And nobody ever voted on them."
    },
    {
      "id": "S10",
      "start": 56.419,
      "speech_end": 58.559,
      "end": 60.959,
      "dur": 4.54,
      "text": "So where exactly do they come from?"
    },
    {
      "id": "S11",
      "start": 60.959,
      "speech_end": 65.014,
      "end": 65.814,
      "dur": 4.855,
      "text": "Start with the honest part. Some of the difference is practical."
    },
    {
      "id": "S12",
      "start": 65.814,
      "speech_end": 70.081,
      "end": 70.881,
      "dur": 5.067,
      "text": "Bodies are shaped differently. Cuts follow shapes. Preferences are real."
    },
    {
      "id": "S13",
      "start": 70.881,
      "speech_end": 75.571,
      "end": 76.371,
      "dur": 5.49,
      "text": "But walk back into that shop and look at what actually separates the two halves of it."
    },
    {
      "id": "S14",
      "start": 76.371,
      "speech_end": 79.485,
      "end": 80.285,
      "dur": 3.915,
      "text": "A different colour. A different pattern. A different label."
    },
    {
      "id": "S14b",
      "start": 80.285,
      "speech_end": 81.875,
      "end": 82.675,
      "dur": 2.39,
      "text": "Or simply a different aisle."
    },
    {
      "id": "S15",
      "start": 82.675,
      "speech_end": 85.285,
      "end": 86.085,
      "dur": 3.41,
      "text": "Does the fabric know which aisle it was hung in?"
    },
    {
      "id": "S16",
      "start": 86.085,
      "speech_end": 90.175,
      "end": 90.975,
      "dur": 4.89,
      "text": "Does a pair of trousers change when somebody carries it across the shop?"
    },
    {
      "id": "S17",
      "start": 90.975,
      "speech_end": 92.298,
      "end": 93.098,
      "dur": 2.123,
      "text": "Of course not."
    },
    {
      "id": "S18",
      "start": 93.098,
      "speech_end": 97.208,
      "end": 99.408,
      "dur": 6.31,
      "text": "The difference is not in the cloth. It is something we added to it."
    },
    {
      "id": "S19",
      "start": 99.408,
      "speech_end": 102.718,
      "end": 103.518,
      "dur": 4.11,
      "text": "Which leaves a better question than who invented all this."
    },
    {
      "id": "S20",
      "start": 103.518,
      "speech_end": 104.728,
      "end": 105.528,
      "dur": 2.01,
      "text": "Who keeps it alive?"
    },
    {
      "id": "S21",
      "start": 105.528,
      "speech_end": 109.378,
      "end": 110.178,
      "dur": 4.65,
      "text": "The answer is not one person. It is not even one industry."
    },
    {
      "id": "S21b",
      "start": 110.178,
      "speech_end": 111.458,
      "end": 112.258,
      "dur": 2.08,
      "text": "It is a loop."
    },
    {
      "id": "S21c",
      "start": 112.258,
      "speech_end": 117.948,
      "end": 119.148,
      "dur": 6.89,
      "text": "By the way, if you like videos like this, consider subscribing. It really helps the channel."
    },
    {
      "id": "S22",
      "start": 119.148,
      "speech_end": 124.588,
      "end": 125.388,
      "dur": 6.24,
      "text": "A manufacturer designs a product. Before anything else, they have to decide who it is for."
    },
    {
      "id": "S23",
      "start": 125.388,
      "speech_end": 130.518,
      "end": 131.318,
      "dur": 5.93,
      "text": "So they look at what people buy. And people buy men's things and women's things."
    },
    {
      "id": "S24",
      "start": 131.318,
      "speech_end": 134.728,
      "end": 135.528,
      "dur": 4.21,
      "text": "So the manufacturer makes men's things and women's things."
    },
    {
      "id": "S25",
      "start": 135.528,
      "speech_end": 142.788,
      "end": 143.588,
      "dur": 8.06,
      "text": "A retailer has to lay out a shop. Customers expect two sections. So the shop gets two sections."
    },
    {
      "id": "S26",
      "start": 143.588,
      "speech_end": 148.298,
      "end": 149.098,
      "dur": 5.51,
      "text": "Marketing has to sell whatever arrives. So it tells us who each thing is for."
    },
    {
      "id": "S26b",
      "start": 149.098,
      "speech_end": 151.402,
      "end": 152.202,
      "dur": 3.104,
      "text": "Men's. Women's. Masculine. Feminine."
    },
    {
      "id": "S27",
      "start": 152.202,
      "speech_end": 155.262,
      "end": 156.062,
      "dur": 3.86,
      "text": "Customers see those categories everywhere they look."
    },
    {
      "id": "S27b",
      "start": 156.062,
      "speech_end": 157.782,
      "end": 158.582,
      "dur": 2.52,
      "text": "And they start to expect them."
    },
    {
      "id": "S28",
      "start": 158.582,
      "speech_end": 162.822,
      "end": 163.622,
      "dur": 5.04,
      "text": "Then manufacturers study those expectations, and design for them."
    },
    {
      "id": "S29",
      "start": 163.622,
      "speech_end": 170.782,
      "end": 171.582,
      "dur": 7.96,
      "text": "Retailers follow the manufacturers. Marketing follows the retailers. People follow the marketing."
    },
    {
      "id": "S29b",
      "start": 171.582,
      "speech_end": 173.042,
      "end": 173.842,
      "dur": 2.26,
      "text": "And around we go."
    },
    {
      "id": "S30",
      "start": 173.842,
      "speech_end": 177.341,
      "end": 178.141,
      "dur": 4.299,
      "text": "People create expectations. Businesses answer them."
    },
    {
      "id": "S30b",
      "start": 178.141,
      "speech_end": 181.411,
      "end": 182.211,
      "dur": 4.07,
      "text": "Businesses reinforce them. People learn them."
    },
    {
      "id": "S31",
      "start": 182.211,
      "speech_end": 186.701,
      "end": 187.501,
      "dur": 5.29,
      "text": "And then the businesses point at the people and say: that is what customers want."
    },
    {
      "id": "S32",
      "start": 187.501,
      "speech_end": 192.041,
      "end": 192.841,
      "dur": 5.34,
      "text": "And the people point at the businesses and say: that is just how things are."
    },
    {
      "id": "S32b",
      "start": 192.841,
      "speech_end": 194.483,
      "end": 195.283,
      "dur": 2.443,
      "text": "And the circle closes."
    },
    {
      "id": "S33",
      "start": 195.283,
      "speech_end": 196.603,
      "end": 197.403,
      "dur": 2.12,
      "text": "So who started it?"
    },
    {
      "id": "S33b",
      "start": 197.403,
      "speech_end": 198.811,
      "end": 199.611,
      "dur": 2.208,
      "text": "Possibly nobody."
    },
    {
      "id": "S34",
      "start": 199.611,
      "speech_end": 205.051,
      "end": 205.851,
      "dur": 6.24,
      "text": "And that is the strange part. A system like this does not need anyone in charge."
    },
    {
      "id": "S34b",
      "start": 205.851,
      "speech_end": 209.021,
      "end": 211.621,
      "dur": 5.77,
      "text": "It only needs everybody to keep taking part in it."
    },
    {
      "id": "S35",
      "start": 211.621,
      "speech_end": 214.331,
      "end": 215.131,
      "dur": 3.51,
      "text": "Which is where the companies come into the story."
    },
    {
      "id": "S36",
      "start": 215.131,
      "speech_end": 221.921,
      "end": 222.721,
      "dur": 7.59,
      "text": "It would be easy to tell it like this. Big firms invented gendered clothing and forced it on the rest of us."
    },
    {
      "id": "S36b",
      "start": 222.721,
      "speech_end": 224.881,
      "end": 225.681,
      "dur": 2.96,
      "text": "That is not really how it works."
    },
    {
      "id": "S37",
      "start": 225.681,
      "speech_end": 229.651,
      "end": 230.451,
      "dur": 4.77,
      "text": "Companies are not standing outside the culture and aiming at it."
    },
    {
      "id": "S37b",
      "start": 230.451,
      "speech_end": 233.861,
      "end": 234.661,
      "dur": 4.21,
      "text": "They are selling things to people who are already inside it."
    },
    {
      "id": "S38",
      "start": 234.661,
      "speech_end": 237.904,
      "end": 238.704,
      "dur": 4.043,
      "text": "They watch what we buy. What we ignore. What we click on."
    },
    {
      "id": "S38b",
      "start": 238.704,
      "speech_end": 241.964,
      "end": 242.764,
      "dur": 4.06,
      "text": "What makes somebody think: that one is for people like me."
    },
    {
      "id": "S39",
      "start": 242.764,
      "speech_end": 247.804,
      "end": 248.604,
      "dur": 5.84,
      "text": "And if splitting a product in two sells more of it, there is every reason to keep going."
    },
    {
      "id": "S40",
      "start": 248.604,
      "speech_end": 253.294,
      "end": 254.094,
      "dur": 5.49,
      "text": "Not because of a grand plan. Sometimes it is simply good business."
    },
    {
      "id": "S40b",
      "start": 254.094,
      "speech_end": 257.154,
      "end": 259.354,
      "dur": 5.26,
      "text": "If a label helps sell the thing, the label stays."
    },
    {
      "id": "S41",
      "start": 259.354,
      "speech_end": 262.294,
      "end": 263.094,
      "dur": 3.74,
      "text": "And marketing can make that split much sharper."
    },
    {
      "id": "S42",
      "start": 263.094,
      "speech_end": 266.486,
      "end": 267.286,
      "dur": 4.192,
      "text": "Take a single product. A razor. A pen. A bicycle."
    },
    {
      "id": "S43",
      "start": 267.286,
      "speech_end": 270.946,
      "end": 271.746,
      "dur": 4.46,
      "text": "One advertisement says: POWER. PERFORMANCE. DURABILITY."
    },
    {
      "id": "S43b",
      "start": 271.746,
      "speech_end": 274.506,
      "end": 275.306,
      "dur": 3.56,
      "text": "Another says: BEAUTY. ELEGANCE. SOFTNESS."
    },
    {
      "id": "S44",
      "start": 275.306,
      "speech_end": 278.316,
      "end": 279.116,
      "dur": 3.81,
      "text": "The same thing. Two completely different promises."
    },
    {
      "id": "S45",
      "start": 279.116,
      "speech_end": 283.876,
      "end": 284.676,
      "dur": 5.56,
      "text": "And suddenly the thing does not just have a function. It has an identity."
    },
    {
      "id": "S45b",
      "start": 284.676,
      "speech_end": 287.016,
      "end": 287.816,
      "dur": 3.14,
      "text": "One we are expected to recognise."
    },
    {
      "id": "S46",
      "start": 287.816,
      "speech_end": 292.556,
      "end": 293.356,
      "dur": 5.54,
      "text": "Sometimes those differences are useful. Sometimes they are genuine."
    },
    {
      "id": "S46b",
      "start": 293.356,
      "speech_end": 296.316,
      "end": 297.116,
      "dur": 3.76,
      "text": "And sometimes the difference is mostly in our heads."
    },
    {
      "id": "S47",
      "start": 297.116,
      "speech_end": 302.286,
      "end": 303.086,
      "dur": 5.97,
      "text": "But once you have seen the same message a few thousand times, it stops feeling like a message."
    },
    {
      "id": "S47b",
      "start": 303.086,
      "speech_end": 305.046,
      "end": 307.446,
      "dur": 4.36,
      "text": "It starts feeling like a fact."
    },
    {
      "id": "S48",
      "start": 307.446,
      "speech_end": 309.176,
      "end": 309.976,
      "dur": 2.53,
      "text": "And this is where we come in."
    },
    {
      "id": "S49",
      "start": 309.976,
      "speech_end": 312.646,
      "end": 313.446,
      "dur": 3.47,
      "text": "Picture a man walking past you in a skirt."
    },
    {
      "id": "S50",
      "start": 313.446,
      "speech_end": 316.636,
      "end": 317.436,
      "dur": 3.99,
      "text": "Something in your head says: that is women's clothing."
    },
    {
      "id": "S50b",
      "start": 317.436,
      "speech_end": 318.951,
      "end": 319.751,
      "dur": 2.315,
      "text": "But why?"
    },
    {
      "id": "S51",
      "start": 319.751,
      "speech_end": 322.791,
      "end": 323.591,
      "dur": 3.84,
      "text": "Nobody ever sat you down and explained the rule."
    },
    {
      "id": "S52",
      "start": 323.591,
      "speech_end": 328.647,
      "end": 329.447,
      "dur": 5.856,
      "text": "You learned it by watching. Your parents. Your classmates. Television. Films. Adverts."
    },
    {
      "id": "S52b",
      "start": 329.447,
      "speech_end": 331.807,
      "end": 332.607,
      "dur": 3.16,
      "text": "Shop windows. Strangers in the street."
    },
    {
      "id": "S53",
      "start": 332.607,
      "speech_end": 333.987,
      "end": 334.787,
      "dur": 2.18,
      "text": "You saw who wore what."
    },
    {
      "id": "S53b",
      "start": 334.787,
      "speech_end": 338.347,
      "end": 339.147,
      "dur": 4.36,
      "text": "And you saw how people reacted when somebody crossed the line."
    },
    {
      "id": "S54",
      "start": 339.147,
      "speech_end": 342.411,
      "end": 343.211,
      "dur": 4.064,
      "text": "So you learned the map. Men over here. Women over there."
    },
    {
      "id": "S55",
      "start": 343.211,
      "speech_end": 347.421,
      "end": 348.221,
      "dur": 5.01,
      "text": "You do not have to think about it any more. It runs by itself."
    },
    {
      "id": "S56",
      "start": 348.221,
      "speech_end": 352.691,
      "end": 353.491,
      "dur": 5.27,
      "text": "And when somebody breaks it, it can feel wrong, even when you cannot say why."
    },
    {
      "id": "S57",
      "start": 353.491,
      "speech_end": 357.051,
      "end": 357.851,
      "dur": 4.36,
      "text": "So the next time you see a man wearing a skirt, don't laugh."
    },
    {
      "id": "S57b",
      "start": 357.851,
      "speech_end": 359.003,
      "end": 359.803,
      "dur": 1.952,
      "text": "Don't stare."
    },
    {
      "id": "S58",
      "start": 359.803,
      "speech_end": 362.213,
      "end": 363.013,
      "dur": 3.21,
      "text": "Ask yourself why it feels unusual."
    },
    {
      "id": "S58b",
      "start": 363.013,
      "speech_end": 365.473,
      "end": 368.273,
      "dur": 5.26,
      "text": "Maybe it's feminine only in our heads."
    },
    {
      "id": "S59",
      "start": 368.273,
      "speech_end": 372.993,
      "end": 373.793,
      "dur": 5.52,
      "text": "Because we have a bad habit. We confuse familiarity with nature."
    },
    {
      "id": "S60",
      "start": 373.793,
      "speech_end": 378.803,
      "end": 379.603,
      "dur": 5.81,
      "text": "Something can feel ancient and obvious simply because we have seen it our whole lives."
    },
    {
      "id": "S61",
      "start": 379.603,
      "speech_end": 384.093,
      "end": 384.893,
      "dur": 5.29,
      "text": "People say men have always worn this. Women have always worn that."
    },
    {
      "id": "S61b",
      "start": 384.893,
      "speech_end": 387.453,
      "end": 389.653,
      "dur": 4.76,
      "text": "So how far back does always actually go?"
    },
    {
      "id": "S62",
      "start": 389.653,
      "speech_end": 395.363,
      "end": 396.163,
      "dur": 6.51,
      "text": "In 1918, an American trade magazine for children's clothing told shops the following."
    },
    {
      "id": "S63",
      "start": 396.163,
      "speech_end": 400.913,
      "end": 401.713,
      "dur": 5.55,
      "text": "Pink is the stronger, more decided colour, so it is more suitable for the boy."
    },
    {
      "id": "S63b",
      "start": 401.713,
      "speech_end": 405.553,
      "end": 406.353,
      "dur": 4.64,
      "text": "Blue is more delicate and dainty, so it is prettier for the girl."
    },
    {
      "id": "S64",
      "start": 406.353,
      "speech_end": 412.473,
      "end": 413.273,
      "dur": 6.92,
      "text": "Exactly the wrong way round, printed as ordinary retail advice, just over a hundred years ago."
    },
    {
      "id": "S64b",
      "start": 413.273,
      "speech_end": 416.713,
      "end": 417.513,
      "dur": 4.24,
      "text": "And before you conclude that everybody did it that way, they didn't."
    },
    {
      "id": "S64c",
      "start": 417.513,
      "speech_end": 423.273,
      "end": 424.073,
      "dur": 6.56,
      "text": "Nine years later, Time magazine listed what the big American department stores were advising."
    },
    {
      "id": "S64d",
      "start": 424.073,
      "speech_end": 428.233,
      "end": 429.033,
      "dur": 4.96,
      "text": "Some said pink for boys. Some said exactly the opposite."
    },
    {
      "id": "S64e",
      "start": 429.033,
      "speech_end": 432.153,
      "end": 432.953,
      "dur": 3.92,
      "text": "They were not following a rule. There wasn't one yet."
    },
    {
      "id": "S64f",
      "start": 432.953,
      "speech_end": 438.123,
      "end": 439.723,
      "dur": 6.77,
      "text": "The version we grew up with did not settle in until about the 1950s."
    },
    {
      "id": "S65",
      "start": 439.723,
      "speech_end": 441.213,
      "end": 442.013,
      "dur": 2.29,
      "text": "Or take high heels."
    },
    {
      "id": "S66",
      "start": 442.013,
      "speech_end": 446.599,
      "end": 447.399,
      "dur": 5.387,
      "text": "They reached Europe from Persia, where cavalry wore them to brace against the stirrups."
    },
    {
      "id": "S67",
      "start": 447.399,
      "speech_end": 451.059,
      "end": 451.859,
      "dur": 4.46,
      "text": "In the 1600s in Europe, a heel was a man's shoe."
    },
    {
      "id": "S67b",
      "start": 451.859,
      "speech_end": 455.269,
      "end": 456.069,
      "dur": 4.21,
      "text": "A sign of status. A sign of masculinity."
    },
    {
      "id": "S67c",
      "start": 456.069,
      "speech_end": 459.479,
      "end": 460.279,
      "dur": 4.21,
      "text": "At the French court, a red heel meant you were close to the king."
    },
    {
      "id": "S67d",
      "start": 460.279,
      "speech_end": 463.039,
      "end": 463.839,
      "dur": 3.56,
      "text": "Nobody at the time thought heels were feminine."
    },
    {
      "id": "S68",
      "start": 463.839,
      "speech_end": 465.098,
      "end": 465.898,
      "dur": 2.059,
      "text": "Or trousers."
    },
    {
      "id": "S68b",
      "start": 465.898,
      "speech_end": 469.408,
      "end": 470.208,
      "dur": 4.31,
      "text": "In ancient Rome, a grown man wore a tunic down to the knee."
    },
    {
      "id": "S68c",
      "start": 470.208,
      "speech_end": 472.149,
      "end": 472.949,
      "dur": 2.741,
      "text": "Bare legs. No trousers."
    },
    {
      "id": "S68d",
      "start": 472.949,
      "speech_end": 476.021,
      "end": 476.821,
      "dur": 3.872,
      "text": "If you saw it in the street today, you would call it a dress."
    },
    {
      "id": "S68e",
      "start": 476.821,
      "speech_end": 480.031,
      "end": 480.831,
      "dur": 4.01,
      "text": "Rome had a line too. It just ran somewhere else."
    },
    {
      "id": "S68f",
      "start": 480.831,
      "speech_end": 487.513,
      "end": 488.313,
      "dur": 7.481,
      "text": "Their line was length. A man's tunic stopped at the knee. A longer one got him called effeminate."
    },
    {
      "id": "S68g",
      "start": 488.313,
      "speech_end": 492.409,
      "end": 493.209,
      "dur": 4.896,
      "text": "And trousers were what foreigners wore. Gauls. Germans. Persians."
    },
    {
      "id": "S68h",
      "start": 493.209,
      "speech_end": 495.869,
      "end": 496.669,
      "dur": 3.46,
      "text": "In 397, that became law."
    },
    {
      "id": "S68i",
      "start": 496.669,
      "speech_end": 501.172,
      "end": 502.772,
      "dur": 6.103,
      "text": "No trousers inside the city of Rome. The penalty was exile."
    },
    {
      "id": "S69",
      "start": 502.772,
      "speech_end": 507.842,
      "end": 508.642,
      "dur": 5.87,
      "text": "Paris had an ordinance requiring a woman to ask the police for permission to wear them."
    },
    {
      "id": "S69b",
      "start": 508.642,
      "speech_end": 512.192,
      "end": 512.992,
      "dur": 4.35,
      "text": "A doctor's note as well. Renewed every six months."
    },
    {
      "id": "S70",
      "start": 512.992,
      "speech_end": 515.211,
      "end": 516.011,
      "dur": 3.019,
      "text": "It was issued in 1800."
    },
    {
      "id": "S70b",
      "start": 516.011,
      "speech_end": 521.069,
      "end": 521.869,
      "dur": 5.858,
      "text": "A French senator asked about it. The government answered in 2013."
    },
    {
      "id": "S71",
      "start": 521.869,
      "speech_end": 525.229,
      "end": 526.029,
      "dur": 4.16,
      "text": "It had quietly lost all force a very long time ago."
    },
    {
      "id": "S71b",
      "start": 526.029,
      "speech_end": 531.189,
      "end": 531.989,
      "dur": 5.96,
      "text": "Not repealed. Just left behind by everything that had changed around it."
    },
    {
      "id": "S71c",
      "start": 531.989,
      "speech_end": 533.899,
      "end": 534.699,
      "dur": 2.71,
      "text": "And yes, that was a real law."
    },
    {
      "id": "S71d",
      "start": 534.699,
      "speech_end": 540.499,
      "end": 541.299,
      "dur": 6.6,
      "text": "You have just seen two of them. One banned trousers. The other made you ask permission."
    },
    {
      "id": "S71e",
      "start": 541.299,
      "speech_end": 543.829,
      "end": 544.629,
      "dur": 3.33,
      "text": "But look at what that one never had to do."
    },
    {
      "id": "S71f",
      "start": 544.629,
      "speech_end": 547.639,
      "end": 548.439,
      "dur": 3.81,
      "text": "It never had to explain why trousers were men's."
    },
    {
      "id": "S71g",
      "start": 548.439,
      "speech_end": 554.099,
      "end": 554.899,
      "dur": 6.46,
      "text": "Everybody already agreed. The law was written on top of something that was there first."
    },
    {
      "id": "S71h",
      "start": 554.899,
      "speech_end": 559.009,
      "end": 559.809,
      "dur": 4.91,
      "text": "Laws like that enforce a convention. They don't invent it."
    },
    {
      "id": "S71i",
      "start": 559.809,
      "speech_end": 562.889,
      "end": 565.489,
      "dur": 5.68,
      "text": "And when the convention moved, the law just sat there."
    },
    {
      "id": "S72",
      "start": 565.489,
      "speech_end": 567.537,
      "end": 568.337,
      "dur": 2.848,
      "text": "Fashion changes constantly."
    },
    {
      "id": "S72b",
      "start": 568.337,
      "speech_end": 572.561,
      "end": 573.361,
      "dur": 5.024,
      "text": "Colours change. Silhouettes change. Hair changes. Shoes change."
    },
    {
      "id": "S73",
      "start": 573.361,
      "speech_end": 575.941,
      "end": 576.741,
      "dur": 3.38,
      "text": "Things that were masculine become feminine."
    },
    {
      "id": "S73b",
      "start": 576.741,
      "speech_end": 579.371,
      "end": 580.171,
      "dur": 3.43,
      "text": "Things that were feminine become masculine."
    },
    {
      "id": "S74",
      "start": 580.171,
      "speech_end": 584.117,
      "end": 584.917,
      "dur": 4.747,
      "text": "The boundaries move. Sometimes slowly. Sometimes very fast."
    },
    {
      "id": "S75",
      "start": 584.917,
      "speech_end": 589.377,
      "end": 591.777,
      "dur": 6.86,
      "text": "And while we are living inside one particular version of them, they feel permanent."
    },
    {
      "id": "S76",
      "start": 591.777,
      "speech_end": 594.687,
      "end": 595.487,
      "dur": 3.71,
      "text": "Now, here is the part that is easy to get wrong."
    },
    {
      "id": "S77",
      "start": 595.487,
      "speech_end": 599.647,
      "end": 600.447,
      "dur": 4.96,
      "text": "Saying that a convention is invented does not make it imaginary."
    },
    {
      "id": "S77b",
      "start": 600.447,
      "speech_end": 602.487,
      "end": 603.287,
      "dur": 2.84,
      "text": "The consequences are very real."
    },
    {
      "id": "S78",
      "start": 603.287,
      "speech_end": 605.877,
      "end": 606.677,
      "dur": 3.39,
      "text": "A man in a skirt can still be laughed at."
    },
    {
      "id": "S78b",
      "start": 606.677,
      "speech_end": 610.767,
      "end": 611.567,
      "dur": 4.89,
      "text": "A woman in something considered masculine can still be judged for it."
    },
    {
      "id": "S79",
      "start": 611.567,
      "speech_end": 614.497,
      "end": 615.297,
      "dur": 3.73,
      "text": "A child can be told that a colour is for girls."
    },
    {
      "id": "S79b",
      "start": 615.297,
      "speech_end": 619.647,
      "end": 620.447,
      "dur": 5.15,
      "text": "An adult can feel embarrassed buying something from the wrong half of the shop."
    },
    {
      "id": "S80",
      "start": 620.447,
      "speech_end": 624.268,
      "end": 625.068,
      "dur": 4.621,
      "text": "None of that is law. No police force enforces it."
    },
    {
      "id": "S80b",
      "start": 625.068,
      "speech_end": 626.924,
      "end": 627.724,
      "dur": 2.656,
      "text": "The enforcement is social."
    },
    {
      "id": "S81",
      "start": 627.724,
      "speech_end": 630.199,
      "end": 630.999,
      "dur": 3.275,
      "text": "Embarrassment. Ridicule. Disapproval."
    },
    {
      "id": "S81b",
      "start": 630.999,
      "speech_end": 632.809,
      "end": 633.609,
      "dur": 2.61,
      "text": "The raised eyebrow. The joke."
    },
    {
      "id": "S82",
      "start": 633.609,
      "speech_end": 635.599,
      "end": 636.399,
      "dur": 2.79,
      "text": "The question: why are you wearing that?"
    },
    {
      "id": "S83",
      "start": 636.399,
      "speech_end": 640.459,
      "end": 643.259,
      "dur": 6.86,
      "text": "And most of the time, just the quiet fear of what other people will think."
    },
    {
      "id": "S84",
      "start": 643.259,
      "speech_end": 648.049,
      "end": 648.849,
      "dur": 5.59,
      "text": "But if all of this is held up by a loop, then the loop can also turn the other way."
    },
    {
      "id": "S85",
      "start": 648.849,
      "speech_end": 652.459,
      "end": 653.259,
      "dur": 4.41,
      "text": "Somebody does something unusual. People see it."
    },
    {
      "id": "S85b",
      "start": 653.259,
      "speech_end": 655.949,
      "end": 656.749,
      "dur": 3.49,
      "text": "And somebody else thinks: actually, I like that."
    },
    {
      "id": "S86",
      "start": 656.749,
      "speech_end": 658.909,
      "end": 659.709,
      "dur": 2.96,
      "text": "They try it. Other people see them."
    },
    {
      "id": "S86b",
      "start": 659.709,
      "speech_end": 662.569,
      "end": 663.369,
      "dur": 3.66,
      "text": "The strange thing becomes slightly less strange."
    },
    {
      "id": "S87",
      "start": 663.369,
      "speech_end": 666.891,
      "end": 667.691,
      "dur": 4.322,
      "text": "More people try it. Shops notice the demand."
    },
    {
      "id": "S87b",
      "start": 667.691,
      "speech_end": 672.121,
      "end": 672.921,
      "dur": 5.23,
      "text": "Manufacturers answer it. Marketing changes its language."
    },
    {
      "id": "S88",
      "start": 672.921,
      "speech_end": 676.331,
      "end": 677.131,
      "dur": 4.21,
      "text": "The thing becomes easier to find, so more people see it."
    },
    {
      "id": "S88b",
      "start": 677.131,
      "speech_end": 681.041,
      "end": 681.841,
      "dur": 4.71,
      "text": "And eventually, what looked ridiculous looks completely ordinary."
    },
    {
      "id": "S89",
      "start": 681.841,
      "speech_end": 683.483,
      "end": 684.283,
      "dur": 2.443,
      "text": "The convention changed."
    },
    {
      "id": "S89b",
      "start": 684.283,
      "speech_end": 687.393,
      "end": 688.193,
      "dur": 3.91,
      "text": "Not because anybody officially changed the rules."
    },
    {
      "id": "S90",
      "start": 688.193,
      "speech_end": 691.783,
      "end": 694.183,
      "dur": 5.99,
      "text": "Because enough people stopped treating the old ones as absolute."
    },
    {
      "id": "S91",
      "start": 694.183,
      "speech_end": 697.623,
      "end": 698.423,
      "dur": 4.24,
      "text": "Which brings us back to the question on the wall of that shop."
    },
    {
      "id": "S91b",
      "start": 698.423,
      "speech_end": 701.083,
      "end": 701.883,
      "dur": 3.46,
      "text": "Is this men's clothing or women's clothing?"
    },
    {
      "id": "S92",
      "start": 701.883,
      "speech_end": 704.673,
      "end": 705.473,
      "dur": 3.59,
      "text": "Sometimes that is simply the wrong question."
    },
    {
      "id": "S92b",
      "start": 705.473,
      "speech_end": 708.913,
      "end": 709.713,
      "dur": 4.24,
      "text": "A better one might be: what is this clothing actually for?"
    },
    {
      "id": "S93",
      "start": 709.713,
      "speech_end": 713.023,
      "end": 713.823,
      "dur": 4.11,
      "text": "Does it fit? Is it comfortable? Does it do the job?"
    },
    {
      "id": "S93b",
      "start": 713.823,
      "speech_end": 716.163,
      "end": 716.963,
      "dur": 3.14,
      "text": "Do you like it? Does it make you feel good?"
    },
    {
      "id": "S94",
      "start": 716.963,
      "speech_end": 720.353,
      "end": 721.153,
      "dur": 4.19,
      "text": "If the answer is yes, what exactly is the label adding?"
    },
    {
      "id": "S95",
      "start": 721.153,
      "speech_end": 723.733,
      "end": 724.533,
      "dur": 3.38,
      "text": "And now the distinction that matters most."
    },
    {
      "id": "S96",
      "start": 724.533,
      "speech_end": 728.243,
      "end": 729.043,
      "dur": 4.51,
      "text": "Nobody is saying that men and women have to dress identically."
    },
    {
      "id": "S96b",
      "start": 729.043,
      "speech_end": 735.943,
      "end": 736.743,
      "dur": 7.7,
      "text": "People are allowed preferences. Cultures are allowed traditions. Fashion is allowed categories."
    },
    {
      "id": "S97",
      "start": 736.743,
      "speech_end": 739.003,
      "end": 739.803,
      "dur": 3.06,
      "text": "There is nothing wrong with any of that."
    },
    {
      "id": "S98",
      "start": 739.803,
      "speech_end": 745.093,
      "end": 745.893,
      "dur": 6.09,
      "text": "The trouble starts when a category stops being a description and turns into a restriction."
    },
    {
      "id": "S99",
      "start": 745.893,
      "speech_end": 749.797,
      "end": 750.597,
      "dur": 4.704,
      "text": "When women's clothing stops meaning clothing usually marketed to women,"
    },
    {
      "id": "S99b",
      "start": 750.597,
      "speech_end": 753.657,
      "end": 754.457,
      "dur": 3.86,
      "text": "and starts meaning clothing you are not allowed to wear."
    },
    {
      "id": "S100",
      "start": 754.457,
      "speech_end": 757.097,
      "end": 757.897,
      "dur": 3.44,
      "text": "Those are two completely different statements."
    },
    {
      "id": "S100b",
      "start": 757.897,
      "speech_end": 762.237,
      "end": 765.237,
      "dur": 7.34,
      "text": "One of them describes a convention. The other one builds a cage."
    },
    {
      "id": "S101",
      "start": 765.237,
      "speech_end": 768.397,
      "end": 769.197,
      "dur": 3.96,
      "text": "So who decides what is men's and what is women's?"
    },
    {
      "id": "S102",
      "start": 769.197,
      "speech_end": 774.81,
      "end": 775.61,
      "dur": 6.413,
      "text": "Manufacturers have a part in it. Retailers have a part. Advertisers have a part."
    },
    {
      "id": "S102b",
      "start": 775.61,
      "speech_end": 777.91,
      "end": 778.71,
      "dur": 3.1,
      "text": "Designers. Our families. Our friends."
    },
    {
      "id": "S103",
      "start": 778.71,
      "speech_end": 780.075,
      "end": 780.875,
      "dur": 2.165,
      "text": "And so do we."
    },
    {
      "id": "S103b",
      "start": 780.875,
      "speech_end": 783.435,
      "end": 784.235,
      "dur": 3.36,
      "text": "Sometimes on purpose. Usually not."
    },
    {
      "id": "S104",
      "start": 784.235,
      "speech_end": 787.895,
      "end": 788.695,
      "dur": 4.46,
      "text": "Which is why there probably isn't a single person to blame."
    },
    {
      "id": "S105",
      "start": 788.695,
      "speech_end": 793.555,
      "end": 794.355,
      "dur": 5.66,
      "text": "There doesn't have to be. The system keeps going because it copies itself."
    },
    {
      "id": "S106",
      "start": 794.355,
      "speech_end": 799.395,
      "end": 800.195,
      "dur": 5.84,
      "text": "We learn the categories. We expect them. Companies answer the expectation."
    },
    {
      "id": "S106b",
      "start": 800.195,
      "speech_end": 804.005,
      "end": 804.805,
      "dur": 4.61,
      "text": "Their products and their advertising teach the categories again."
    },
    {
      "id": "S107",
      "start": 804.805,
      "speech_end": 807.385,
      "end": 808.185,
      "dur": 3.38,
      "text": "And the next generation learns them from us."
    },
    {
      "id": "S107b",
      "start": 808.185,
      "speech_end": 809.615,
      "end": 812.215,
      "dur": 4.029,
      "text": "Round and round."
    },
    {
      "id": "S108",
      "start": 812.215,
      "speech_end": 815.005,
      "end": 815.805,
      "dur": 3.59,
      "text": "But a convention has one enormous weakness."
    },
    {
      "id": "S109",
      "start": 815.805,
      "speech_end": 819.165,
      "end": 819.965,
      "dur": 4.16,
      "text": "It only works as long as people believe that it matters."
    },
    {
      "id": "S110",
      "start": 819.965,
      "speech_end": 822.805,
      "end": 823.605,
      "dur": 3.64,
      "text": "Which means you don't have to bring the whole thing down."
    },
    {
      "id": "S110b",
      "start": 823.605,
      "speech_end": 825.765,
      "end": 826.565,
      "dur": 2.96,
      "text": "You don't have to convince anybody."
    },
    {
      "id": "S111",
      "start": 826.565,
      "speech_end": 830.075,
      "end": 830.875,
      "dur": 4.31,
      "text": "You don't even have to stop wearing men's or women's clothing."
    },
    {
      "id": "S112",
      "start": 830.875,
      "speech_end": 834.365,
      "end": 835.165,
      "dur": 4.29,
      "text": "You only have to remember what these categories actually are."
    },
    {
      "id": "S113",
      "start": 835.165,
      "speech_end": 836.675,
      "end": 837.475,
      "dur": 2.31,
      "text": "They are conventions."
    },
    {
      "id": "S113b",
      "start": 837.475,
      "speech_end": 840.815,
      "end": 841.615,
      "dur": 4.14,
      "text": "Not laws. Not physics. Not biology. Not morality."
    },
    {
      "id": "S113c",
      "start": 841.615,
      "speech_end": 842.915,
      "end": 845.115,
      "dur": 3.5,
      "text": "Just conventions."
    },
    {
      "id": "S114",
      "start": 845.115,
      "speech_end": 849.445,
      "end": 850.245,
      "dur": 5.131,
      "text": "And if one day you wear something that convention says belongs to the other side,"
    },
    {
      "id": "S115",
      "start": 850.245,
      "speech_end": 855.745,
      "end": 856.545,
      "dur": 6.3,
      "text": "you haven't committed a crime. You haven't broken reality. You haven't hurt anybody."
    },
    {
      "id": "S116",
      "start": 856.545,
      "speech_end": 858.455,
      "end": 859.255,
      "dur": 2.71,
      "text": "You crossed an invisible line."
    },
    {
      "id": "S117",
      "start": 859.255,
      "speech_end": 861.715,
      "end": 862.515,
      "dur": 3.26,
      "text": "And maybe the line was never really there."
    },
    {
      "id": "S117b",
      "start": 862.515,
      "speech_end": 866.155,
      "end": 866.955,
      "dur": 4.44,
      "text": "Maybe we just kept drawing it. Over and over again."
    },
    {
      "id": "S118",
      "start": 866.955,
      "speech_end": 870.095,
      "end": 872.695,
      "dur": 5.74,
      "text": "Until we forgot that we were the ones holding the pencil."
    },
    {
      "id": "S119",
      "start": 872.695,
      "speech_end": 875.255,
      "end": 876.055,
      "dur": 3.36,
      "text": "And if you ever see a skirt you actually like,"
    },
    {
